<H1> introduction to biology </H1>
<p><b>biology</b> is the branch of science that deals with the study of life and living organisms. It helps us understand humans, animals, plants, microorganisms, and how they interact with their environment. </p>
<h2> main branches of biology </h2>
<P><b>botany<br>
zoology<br>
microbiology<br>
genetics<br>
human biology </b>
<h2> characteristics of biology</h2>
<P><b>Movement</b>: They can move or show movement.<br>

<b>Respiration</b> They release energy from food.<br>

<B>Nutrition</B>: They need food for energy and growth.<br>

<b>Growth</B>: They increase in size and develop.<br>

<B>Reproduction</B>: They produce new organisms.<br>

<B>Excretion</B>: They remove waste materials.<br>

<B>Sensitivity</B>: They respond to changes in their surroundings.</P>
<H2>important topics of biology</H2>
<P><b>Cell Biology</B>: Study of cells.<br>

<b>Anatomy</b>: Study of body structure.<br>

<b>Physiology</b>: Study of how the body works.<br>

<b>Ecology</b>: Study of organisms and their environment.<br>

<B>Evolution</B>: Study of how living organisms change over generations.<BR>

<b>Molecular Biology</b>: Study of biological molecules such as DNA and proteins.</P>
<h2> WHY IS BIOLOGY IMPORTANT ?</h2>
<p>Biology helps us:

Understand the human body.<br>

Discover medicines and treatments.<br>

Improve agriculture and food production<br>.

Protect plants and animals.<br>

Understand diseases and infections.<br>

Protect the environment and biodiversity<br></p>
